// LLAMP-SPEC v1 | ADR-057
=adr: 057
=title: Platform System Health API
=date: 2026-04-06
=status: accepted

#ctx
~operators need live visibility into infrastructure: NATS, Redis, BullMQ, MongoDB, gateways
~no current health aggregation endpoint beyond Fastify default /healthz
~existing singleton managers already track internal state — no new DB models needed

#opts
~a: poll each subsystem independently from frontend (N separate calls, no RBAC)
~b: single aggregated GET /api/v1/health/system backend endpoint (RBAC-gated)

#decision
~b: GET /api/v1/health/system (SuperAdmin + Admin RBAC only)
~aggregates from existing singleton managers — NO new DB models
~subsystems: NATS stream stats, Redis ping+memoryUsage, BullMQ queue counts, MongoDB isMaster, gateway counts per type
~frontend: /system-health page, 30s auto-poll, per-subsystem status card (green/amber/red)
~HealthController added as 15th controller; registered in server.ts

#consequences
~+1 endpoint; +1 controller; each manager exposes .getStatus() or equivalent read method
~read-only; no write path; no DB schema changes
~gateway managers expose connectedCount (already tracked internally)
~subsystem status: green=ok, amber=degraded (high latency/queue backlog), red=unreachable

#scope
~arch_summary_update: yes
